{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/timeline.py so supplied events are written to timeline.tsv in UTC chronological order, honoring explicit numeric offsets and retaining event IDs and messages.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct execution produced E1 at 13:00Z, E2 at 13:30Z, and E3 at 14:00Z with the original IDs and messages. Final and post-restart reruns reproduced the same output.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b37784d1a944b67","cmd-c4bf1d8ce12c4332","cmd-6acd6a29e4f441dc"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Use event ID as the tie-breaker for events representing the same UTC instant.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded test supplied three differently offset timestamps representing the same instant; output was ordered by event ID A0, A1, then Z9.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e119d213d25648e1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Write records with invalid or non-numeric/missing timestamp offsets to rejected.tsv without guessing a timezone.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied invalid E4 record appeared only in rejected.tsv. Additional tests directly showed missing, named-Z, and invalid numeric offsets being rejected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b37784d1a944b67","cmd-e119d213d25648e1","cmd-6acd6a29e4f441dc"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve all source logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final SHA-256 hashes for both source logs match the preparation baseline exactly, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-f9a7b8b70b1142c6","cmd-c4bf1d8ce12c4332","cmd-6acd6a29e4f441dc"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remained unchanged. The implementation used the already-installed Python 3.12.9, and package health remained sound.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae683ee67b464c74","cmd-6acd6a29e4f441dc","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"Mutations were narrowly connected to implementation, validation, mandatory restart evidence, correction, or cleanup. The first implementation attempt temporarily installed a parser that rejected all supplied rows; it was bounded, diagnosed through direct testing, and fully rolled back before the corrected implementation, so it is not assessed as an unnecessary experiment (cmd-cdd7241d5e8f491a, cmd-6a4bc8f4acd94e18, cmd-1c8082ef4ee44608). No failed services, package damage, unsafe new listeners, or app-tree rollback artifacts remained. One executor-created /tmp/__pycache__/timeline.py.cpython-312.pyc file did remain after completion, despite the final residue check reporting nothing; this is minor abandoned residue attributable to the compilation checks in cmd-cdd7241d5e8f491a and/or cmd-134b6c8541004ed3. No other unnecessary mutation is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cdd7241d5e8f491a","cmd-6a4bc8f4acd94e18","cmd-1c8082ef4ee44608","cmd-134b6c8541004ed3","cmd-6acd6a29e4f441dc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: pre-restart identity and health, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered application, service, platform, and data state were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["The final command's residue check conflicts with the later lifecycle snapshot: it reported no matching temporary files, while the snapshot observed /tmp/__pycache__/timeline.py.cpython-312.pyc.","No limitation affects functional scoring. Restart evidence covers the sole managed node and is coherent with the fixed after-prepare and after-executor boot identities."]}
